# Enum Boolean Getters

**Rule:** Do not compare an enum value against a specific case with `==` at the
call site. Instead, define `bool get isX` getters inside the enum (one per case)
and compare through them. This keeps comparison logic encapsulated in the enum,
reads naturally, and makes call sites resilient if cases are renamed.

### ✅ Good Example
```dart
enum AppAuthStatus {
  initial,
  authenticated,
  unauthenticated;

  bool get isInitial => this == AppAuthStatus.initial;
  bool get isAuthenticated => this == AppAuthStatus.authenticated;
  bool get isUnauthenticated => this == AppAuthStatus.unauthenticated;
}

// call site
final loggedIn = authCubit.state.status.isAuthenticated;
```

### ❌ Bad Example
```dart
enum AppAuthStatus {
  initial,
  authenticated,
  unauthenticated,
}

// call site
final loggedIn = authCubit.state.status == AppAuthStatus.authenticated;
```
